course: dictionary
lesson: 8081
title: Remain: what is left and what stays
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To remain means to stay, or to still be there after other things have gone. «Two cakes remain» means two cakes are left after everyone has eaten the rest. You can use it for people too: «Please remain seated» means stay in your seat.
explain: In maths, the remainder is what is left over after dividing. 13 divided by 4 is 3 with 1 left over, so the remainder is 1. When you see remain in a maths problem, ask yourself: what is still left at the end?
explain: Remains is also a noun. «Megalodon was a huge shark from about 23 to 3.6 million years ago» and its skeleton was cartilage, which rarely fossilises, so mostly teeth remain. Those teeth are the remains that scientists find.
explain: Use context to check. In «What remains of a Sun-like star is a white dwarf», remains means what is left after the rest has gone. Swap in left and read it again: it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: To remain means to stay, or to still be there after other things have gone.
fact: «Remains» can mean what is left of something, such as old bones or ruins.
fact: In maths, the remainder is what is left over after dividing: 13 ÷ 4 = 3 remainder 1.
fact: «Remain calm» means stay calm, and «remain in your seat» means stay in your seat.
fact: Scientists often find the remains of animals from long ago, such as fossilised teeth of the megalodon shark.
exercise: There are six biscuits and four are eaten. «How many biscuits remain?» | *Two | Ten | Six | Four
exercise: «Please remain seated.» What does this ask you to do? | Stand up and leave | Run around the room | Sit on the floor | *Stay in your seat
exercise: 13 divided by 4 is 3 with what remainder? | *1 | 13 | 4 | 3
test: «Only three crayons remain in the box.» What does remain mean here? | To be lost forever | *To be left | To be painted | To be heavy
test: Scientists study the remains of a shark. What are remains? | A kind of food | A fast swimming race | *What is left, such as old bones | Shiny jewels
exam: «Let no debt remain outstanding.» What does remain mean here? | Pay back quickly | *Stay or be left | Grow bigger | Vanish suddenly
